From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wayland-workspace: Show the workspaces of the panel's output

The Wayland switcher listed every workspace the compositor has, whatever
group it is in. A compositor that gives each output workspaces of its own
has an ext-workspace group for each output, so a switcher there had a
button for each workspace of each output, with one active button for each
output, and no way to tell whose a button was.

Where the panel names its output, which it does under Caminito, the
Wayland compositor, show the workspaces of the group that output is in. A
click then switches that output, the scroll wheel moves through that
output's workspaces, and the preferences count and name them. The buttons
are built again when the panel moves to another output, which maps its
surface again, when the switcher moves to another panel, and when a group's
outputs change.

Where the panel names no output, or no group has that output, the switcher
lists every workspace, as before. With one group for every output, the
group's workspaces are every workspace, so nothing changes there.

The applet now uses gtk-layer-shell, which the panel it is loaded into
links already.
